#
# holt — Swift for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Swift symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Swift`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Swift parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Swift\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Swift ######################################################################
--langdef=HoltSwift
--map-HoltSwift=+.swift
--kinddef-HoltSwift=f,function,functions
--kinddef-HoltSwift=c,class,classes and protocols
--kinddef-HoltSwift=v,variable,variables
--regex-HoltSwift=/^[ \t]*(public|private|internal|open|fileprivate|static|final|override|mutating|[ \t])*func[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\2/f/
--regex-HoltSwift=/^[ \t]*(public|private|internal|open|final|indirect|[ \t])*(class|struct|enum|protocol|actor|extension)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\3/c/
--regex-HoltSwift=/^[ \t]*(public|private|internal|open|static|[ \t])*(let|var)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\3/v/
